#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the Jibb desks on a fake ship: start it, sync desks, run the tests.

    tools/ship start                 start the fake ship in the background
    tools/ship stop                  stop it
    tools/ship status                running or not; desks, revisions, mounts
    tools/ship sync my-app           assemble a desk from its folders, |commit
    tools/ship test                  sync the jibb-dev test desk, run -test
    tools/ship gen-tests             write tests/lib/jibb.hoon from tests/golden
    tools/ship check-commit          prove that |commit stores .jibb files
    tools/ship scry /cx/=my-app=/ui/about/jibb
    tools/ship hoon '(add 2 2)'      evaluate Hoon on the ship, as dojo would
    tools/ship run FILE              run a thread file (a strand) on the ship
    tools/ship poke hood kiln-commit '[%my-app |]'
    tools/ship commit|mount|unmount DESK
    tools/ship log                   the end of the ship's log

The ship is a fake ~zod at /root/urbit/zod (--pier or $JIBB_PIER), run
with -t in its own session, its output going to <pier>.log (--log or
$JIBB_SHIP_LOG); a start moves the previous log to <pier>.log.1.

Commands reach the ship over its conn.sock, as khan-eval threads: click
(/root/src/tools/pkg/click/click, --click or $JIBB_CLICK) formats and
jams each request, and this script sends it and reads the whole reply.
It doesn't let click do the sending, because click reads the reply with
`nc -U -W 1`, which stops after the first 16 KB, so bigger replies came
back cut off and decoded to garbage.  click's -i quoting escapes only
single quotes and joins the lines with gaps, so threads are written
without comments and their backslashes are doubled before click sees
them.

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 when something failed (a commit, a test, a
check), 2 when the command couldn't run (a usage error, no ship).
"""

